%Examples in the literature of FEM meshes for problems involving cavities where the mesh width is much smaller inside the cavity include, e.g., \cite[Figure 7]{MoSu:98}. To our knowledge, the present paper is the first to design meshes that take into account the global effects in Item 2 (and, moreover, in a frequency-explicit way).
