be the associated weighted adjacency matrix. Here, 
\beqs
h_{\min}(N) = \begin{pmatrix}
0 & h_{\visible,\pml}^N & h_{\invisible,\pml}^N & h_{\pml}^N
\end{pmatrix}^T.
\eeqs
 The point is that $\mathscr{T}$ is, up to a constant, the simple-path matrix of $\mathscr{W}$. More precisely, the following result holds.


