\subsection{Motion from real images}
In this section, we manually selected points that appear to be on the crater rim of real pushbroom images captured by the LRO NAC cameras \cite{Robinson:2010}, and we used these points to recover the state of the spacecraft. Crater rims are not always well-defined, and the user choice of which points belong to the rim has an impact on the accuracy.

