\subsection{Champion Basics} \label{app:championbasics}
In games, each player steers independent control on in-game avatar called a \emph{champion}. League of Legends features 169 unique playable champions, each with their own unique set of abilities. Such abilities can be used to deal damage, heal, shield or cast other effects to enemy or ally champions. Each champion is also equipped with 2 set of summoner spells, which provide various effects and utilities such as healing, shielding, slowing, transporting, etc. A champion requires \emph{Health Points} to stay alive. A dead champion is re-spawned after a certain interval of time. Champions require \emph{mana} points to cast their abilities. Items are purchased using gold. As champions gain experience and level-up, the magnitude of their abilities and base statistics rise. Figure~\ref{fig:champion_details} shows an in-game champion with its set of abilities, spells and item crafting.

