\section{Proof of Theorem~\ref{thm:converge}}\label{apx:converge}
%\noindent\emph{Proof of Theorem~\ref{thm:converge}.}
The proof of Theorem~\ref{thm:converge} follows a similar trajectory to the convergence proof of relative value iteration (RVI) $Q$-learning presented by Abounadi~\cite{abounadi2001learning}. The key difference is that we now need to show the asymptotic stability of the structural update rules~\eqref{eq:primal}-\eqref{eq:dual}.

Define the following function:
\begin{equation*}
\begin{aligned}
\mathcal{H}_{\phi,a}(\bm Q)\triangleq r(\phi,a)&+\sum_{\phi'\in\mathbb{S}}\mathbb{P}(\phi'|\phi,a)\max_{a'\in\mathbb{A}_{\phi'}}Q(\phi',a')\\
			&-Q(\phi,a)-Q(\phi_f,a_f).
\end{aligned}
\end{equation*}
%
According to~\cite[Theorem 3.4]{abounadi2001learning}, the ordinary differential equation (ODE) for RVI $Q$-learning, denoted as $\dot{\bm Q}=\mathcal{H}(\bm Q)$, is gobally asymptotically stable at the equilibrium $\hat{\bm Q}$. Consequently, ${\bm Q}^T\mathcal{H}(\bm Q)<0$ holds for all points except $\hat{\bm Q}$.

For the structural updates~\eqref{eq:primal}-\eqref{eq:dual}, the corresponding ODE is given by

\begin{equation}\label{eq:ode}
\dot{\bm Q}	=\mathcal{\bm H}(\bm Q)+\bm{T}^T\bm{\nu},\qquad \dot{\bm{\nu}}	=-\bm{TQ}.
\end{equation}
To establish the convergence of this ODE, we construct the Lyapunov function $\mathcal{V}(\bm{Q},\bm{\nu})=\frac{1}{2}\bm{Q}^T\bm{Q}+\frac{1}{2}\bm{\nu}^T\bm{\nu}$. Then
\begin{equation*}
\dot{\mathcal{V}}=\bm{Q}^T(\mathcal{\bm H}(\bm Q)+\bm{T}^T\bm{\nu})-\bm{\nu}^T\bm{TQ}=\bm{Q}^T\mathcal{H}(\bm Q)<0,
\end{equation*}
for all points except $\hat{\bm Q}$. Therefore, \eqref{eq:ode} is globally asymptotically stable, and thus~\eqref{eq:primal}-\eqref{eq:dual} converge to the solution to~\eqref{eq:q update} almost surely. %\hfill$\Box$

