\textbf{Benchmark Circuits}\quad{}
We used six types of benchmark circuits in our evaluations.
\begin{itemize}
    \item Quantum Fourier Transform (QFT)~\cite{shor1994algorithms}.
    \item Alternating Layered Ansatz (ALA)~\cite{cerezo2021cost}.
    \item Random Quantum Circuit (RQC)~\cite{boixo2018characterizing}.
    \item Quantum Volume Circuit (QVC)~\cite{cross2019validating}.
    \item Instantaneous Quantum Polynomial (IQP)~\cite{bremner2017achieving}.
    \item Hamiltonian Evolution Simulation (HES)~\cite{low2017optimal}.
\end{itemize}

Among the six types of circuits, QFT, RQC, IQP, and HES are relatively more sparse. So we call them \emph{sparse-class} benchmarks. Correspondingly, ALA and QVC consist of mostly dense single-qubit gates, so we call them \emph{dense-class} benchmarks.
