%%
While the search space is exponential in the number of piles ($2^\numpile$ possible assignments),
\cite{treleaven2025sortingpermutationspileshuffle} showed
that
a minimal sort can be obtained, if one exists,
in time that is linear in the permutation length,
by
%a two-equation recurrence
combining~\eqref{eq:min-piles-mixed} with
a greedy strategy for choosing a minimizing types assignment $\pileType^*$.




