\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
For each of the three aligned cases,
the claims are fairly easy to reason by repeated application of Lemma~\ref{lemma:align-singleton}.
%
For the final case we observe that
starting from $\bStart \backslash k_1$ and 
applying $6n+1$ copies of $\gtAlign$,
we find ourselves at a state
\begin{align*}
\geq \, (\bStart+6n+1) \backslash (k_1 + 2(6n+1))
&= (\bStart+1) \backslash \left( k_1 + 2(6n+1) + n \right)
