It is fairly straightforward then to augment the second and third rounds of sort:
%
We may easily increase the number of piles in the second round
by introducing arbitrarily many unused dummy variables.
%
Similarly, we may increase the number of piles in the third round
by introducing ineffectual clauses, \eg,
adding additional copies of any clauses already in the formula.
All we need then is a strategy to augment the first round.

%
Suppose we widen the first round by repetition, \ie, using $\designAlign^k$ for some $k \geq 1$.
