    In the billiards-inspired task, a Franka Research 3 (FR3) robot is positioned on a flat surface. In each scene, a cue ball is placed in front of the robot within a defined region, while a target billiard ball and a goal position are randomly sampled elsewhere in the scene. Several obstacles representing common household objects (e.g., toys, dishware, decor) of varied geometry and material are randomly selected from the photorealistic asset library in Nvidia Omniverse and scattered throughout the workspace. Entities in the scene, including the robot and floor, are manually assigned realistic physical parameters, such as friction, restitution, and mass, to ensure realistic behavior. We reconstruct each scene using 60 images, with optimization averaging 3 seconds per frame for a total mapping time of around 3 minutes.

